      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under N2, iodine was added to a slurry of La metal in dry MeCN and stirred for 1 h. 2,6-Di-tert-butyl-4-methylphenol was added and the mixture was sonicated for 2 days, filtered, concentrated to 5 mL, and cooled to −6 °C. After one week, colourless crystals were collected, washed with hexane, and dried under vacuum. An RTP comparison used La filings, Hg(C6F5)2 and the phenol in MeCN with overnight sonication.",
