        "procedure": "A reduced excess of Eu metal was stirred with 2,6-diphenylphenol, Hg(C6F5)2 and one drop of Hg in thf at ambient temperature for 3 days. After filtration and concentration to 5 mL, dme (10 mL) and toluene (5 mL) were added and the solution was reconcentrated. After 2 days at ambient temperature a mixture of orange rods of [Eu(Odpp)3(dme)] and yellow/orange rhombic crystals of [Eu(Odpp)2(dme)2] precipitated; the compounds were hand-picked for X-ray crystallography and could not be separated for bulk characterization.",
